// Issue-validation golden set. One case per line: { id, tags, input: { title, body }, expected: { valid, score_min?, score_max?, blockers? } }.
// Lines starting with // are comments. Labels follow prompts/validation-system.md (B1–B4 blockers, score >= 70).
// expected.blockers lists the rule codes a targeted case must be rejected for (blocker_match scorer); omitted when several rules can fairly apply.
// Only cases the LLM judges: deterministic guards (e.g. a tag-only title, short-circuited by isMeaningfulTitle) are unit-tested, not evaluated.
// --- core: the original 15 cases. `--tags core` keeps a series comparable with runs before the dataset grew. ---
{"id":"valid-api-endpoint","tags":["valid","api","core"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Add GET /health endpoint","body":"## Context\nAdd a health endpoint to `src/server.mjs` (Express app).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `GET /health` returns HTTP 200 with JSON body `{ \"status\": \"ok\" }`\n- [ ] Response has `Content-Type: application/json`\n- [ ] `POST /health` returns HTTP 405\n- [ ] A test in `test/health.test.mjs` covers both cases\n\n## Out of scope\nDependency checks (DB, cache)."},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
{"id":"valid-pure-function","tags":["valid","lib","core"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Add slugify helper","body":"Add `slugify(text)` to `scripts/lib/strings.mjs`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `slugify('Hello World')` returns `'hello-world'`\n- [ ] Consecutive non-alphanumeric characters collapse to one `-`\n- [ ] Leading/trailing `-` are trimmed\n- [ ] `slugify('')` returns `''`\n- [ ] `slugify(null)` throws `TypeError`\n- [ ] Unit tests in `scripts/tests/strings.test.mjs` cover each item"},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
{"id":"valid-bugfix","tags":["valid","bug","core"],"input":{"title":"[BUG] parseFlatYaml drops values containing a colon","body":"## Bug\n`parseFlatYaml` in `scripts/lib/yaml.mjs` splits on every `:`, so `url: https://x.dev` parses as `https`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `parseFlatYaml('url: https://x.dev')` returns `{ url: 'https://x.dev' }`\n- [ ] Keys without a value still parse to `''`\n- [ ] Existing tests in `scripts/tests/yaml.test.mjs` still pass\n- [ ] A regression test covers the colon-in-value case"},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
{"id":"valid-docs-diagram","tags":["valid","docs","core"],"input":{"title":"[DOCS] Add pipeline Mermaid diagram to README","body":"Add a Mermaid flowchart to `README.md` under a new `## Pipeline` section.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `README.md` contains a `## Pipeline` section with a ```mermaid block\n- [ ] The diagram has nodes labeled Issue Validation, Code Generation, PR Review, Auto-fix, Human Merge\n- [ ] Directed edges connect them in that order, plus Auto-fix → PR Review\n- [ ] No other README section is modified\n\nGitHub renders Mermaid natively; no tooling required."},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
{"id":"valid-config-change","tags":["valid","config","core"],"input":{"title":"[CHORE] Raise validation_max_tokens to 1536","body":"## Change\nIn `config/models.yaml`, set `validation_max_tokens: 1536` (currently 1024) because reasoning tokens truncate the JSON output.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `config/models.yaml` has `validation_max_tokens:  1536`\n- [ ] `loadLLMConfig('validation').maxTokens === 1536` (assert in `scripts/tests/config.test.mjs`)\n- [ ] No other key in `config/models.yaml` changes"},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
{"id":"valid-error-handling","tags":["valid","edge","core"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] readCheckpoint returns null on corrupt JSON","body":"`readCheckpoint` in `scripts/lib/checkpoint.mjs` currently throws on a corrupt checkpoint file.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] When the file contains invalid JSON, `readCheckpoint` returns `null`\n- [ ] When the file is missing, it still returns `null`\n- [ ] When the file is valid, the parsed object is returned unchanged\n- [ ] A warning is logged via `logger.error` with the file path on corrupt JSON\n- [ ] Tests cover all three cases"},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
{"id":"invalid-no-ac","tags":["invalid","b1","core"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Add dark mode","body":"Users want dark mode. Please add it."},"expected":{"valid":false,"score_max":69}}
{"id":"invalid-vague-ac","tags":["invalid","b1","core"],"input":{"title":"[BUG] Login is broken","body":"Login doesn't work sometimes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Fix the bug\n- [ ] It should work correctly"},"expected":{"valid":false,"score_max":69}}
{"id":"invalid-subjective-ac","tags":["invalid","b2","core"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Redesign settings page","body":"Redesign `src/pages/Settings.tsx`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The page looks modern and clean\n- [ ] Users find it intuitive\n- [ ] It feels responsive"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
{"id":"invalid-unmeasurable-perf","tags":["invalid","b2","core"],"input":{"title":"[PERF] Speed up PR review","body":"`scripts/pr_review.mjs` is slow.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Review should be faster\n- [ ] Better performance overall"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
{"id":"invalid-ambiguous-scope","tags":["invalid","b3","core"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Add caching","body":"We should cache things to reduce load.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Responses are cached\n- [ ] Cache hit returns the cached value"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
{"id":"invalid-arch-choice","tags":["invalid","b3","core"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Persist pipeline metrics","body":"Metrics should be stored somewhere durable, either Postgres or Redis, whatever fits.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Metrics survive a restart\n- [ ] Metrics can be queried"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
{"id":"invalid-undocumented-dependency","tags":["invalid","b4","core"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Post review summary to Slack","body":"After each review, send the verdict to Slack through the notifier service the platform team is building. It is not deployed yet and has no published endpoint or API contract.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `pr_review.mjs` calls the notifier with `{ prNumber, verdict }`\n- [ ] A Slack message appears in #dev-loop"},"expected":{"valid":false}}
{"id":"invalid-empty-body","tags":["invalid","b1","edge","core"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Improve logging","body":""},"expected":{"valid":false,"score_max":69}}
{"id":"invalid-problem-only","tags":["invalid","b1","core"],"input":{"title":"[BUG] Auto-fix loops forever on PR #42","body":"On PR #42 the auto-fix workflow kept pushing commits for an hour. Logs attached in the run. Something is wrong with the attempt counter in `scripts/auto_fix_pr.mjs`."},"expected":{"valid":false}}
// --- Discriminating edge cases. Tags: partial-ac, role-scope, scope-pair, stub (B4 minimal pair), short, fr, warnings-only, injection. ---
// B2 "Dependent on undefined human judgment": "the existing error style" is written down nowhere, so no test can assert it.
{"id":"invalid-partial-ac-style","tags":["invalid","b2","partial-ac"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Validate config/labels.yaml on load","body":"`loadLabels()` in `scripts/lib/config.mjs` accepts any YAML today.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A label without `name` throws `Error` naming the line number\n- [ ] A `color` that is not 6 hex digits throws `Error` naming the label\n- [ ] Duplicate label names throw `Error` listing both occurrences\n- [ ] Error messages follow the existing error style of `scripts/lib/`\n- [ ] Tests in `scripts/tests/config.test.mjs` cover the three error cases"},"expected":{"valid":false,"blockers":["B2"]}}
// B2 "Unmeasurable": neither the directory size nor the time limit is defined, so "without timing out" has no pass condition.
{"id":"invalid-partial-ac-no-threshold","tags":["invalid","b2","partial-ac"],"input":{"title":"[PERF] Cache prompts in loadPrompt","body":"`loadPrompt(name)` in `scripts/lib/prompts.mjs` reads the file on every call.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A second `loadPrompt('validation-system')` call does not call `fs.readFileSync` (asserted with a mock)\n- [ ] The cached value is identical to the first returned string\n- [ ] A missing file still throws `Prompt file not found`\n- [ ] Loading works for large prompt directories without timing out"},"expected":{"valid":false,"blockers":["B2"]}}
// B2: "most relevant" has no ranking definition; two engineers would write different assertions. A B3 reading ("relevant" undefined) is possible, hence blocker_match is not gated.
{"id":"invalid-partial-ac-relevance","tags":["invalid","b2","partial-ac"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Search past validation reports","body":"Add `searchReports(query)` to `scripts/lib/report_search.mjs`, over the JSON reports in `observability/reports/`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `searchReports('')` throws `TypeError`\n- [ ] Results are `{ issueNumber, score }` objects\n- [ ] At most 10 results are returned\n- [ ] The 10 most relevant reports for the query are returned\n- [ ] Tests in `scripts/tests/report_search.test.mjs` cover each item"},"expected":{"valid":false,"blockers":["B2"]}}
// B2: "tous les modèles courants" names no list, so no test can check coverage.
{"id":"invalid-fr-partial-ac","tags":["invalid","b2","partial-ac","fr"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Ajouter un résumé des coûts au rapport d'évals","body":"Ajouter une section `## Coût` au rapport Markdown produit par `scripts/lib/eval_harness.mjs`.\n\n## Critères d'acceptation\n- [ ] La section affiche `tokens_est` total et par cas\n- [ ] La section est absente quand `tokens_est` vaut 0\n- [ ] Le coût en dollars est calculé pour tous les modèles courants\n- [ ] Un test dans `scripts/tests/eval_harness.test.mjs` vérifie chaque point"},"expected":{"valid":false,"blockers":["B2"]}}
// B3 "scope boundary unclear (… all users or a specific role?)": endpoints are explicit, who may call PATCH/DELETE is not.
{"id":"invalid-role-ambiguous","tags":["invalid","b3","role-scope"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Project member management endpoints","body":"Add member management to the Express API in `src/routes/projects.mjs`.\n\n## Endpoints\n- `GET /api/projects/:id/members` — list members\n- `PATCH /api/projects/:id/members/:userId` — change a member's role\n- `DELETE /api/projects/:id/members/:userId` — remove a member\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `GET` returns 200 with `[{ userId, role }]`\n- [ ] `PATCH` and `DELETE` return 403 for users who are not allowed to manage members\n- [ ] `DELETE` on an unknown member returns 404\n- [ ] Tests in `test/projects.test.mjs` cover each status code"},"expected":{"valid":false,"blockers":["B3"]}}
// B3 "Key terms are undefined and could mean multiple incompatible things": "admins" maps to two existing roles.
{"id":"invalid-role-two-admin-roles","tags":["invalid","b3","role-scope"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Restrict audit log export to admins","body":"`GET /api/audit/export` in `src/routes/audit.mjs` is open to every authenticated user. The app has two admin roles today: `org_admin` and `project_admin` (scoped to one project).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Admins get 200 with a CSV body\n- [ ] Other authenticated users get 403\n- [ ] Anonymous requests get 401\n- [ ] Tests cover the three responses"},"expected":{"valid":false,"blockers":["B3"]}}
// Scope pair, closed side. Not B3: every file is listed, local is pinned to debug, so "deployed" is the closed complement (preview, staging, production). One diff. Anti-over-strictness case.
{"id":"valid-scope-environment-closed","tags":["valid","b3","scope-pair"],"input":{"title":"[CHORE] Disable debug logging in deployed environments","body":"`LOG_LEVEL=debug` leaks request bodies. `config/env/` holds `local.yaml`, `preview.yaml`, `staging.yaml`, `production.yaml`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `LOG_LEVEL` is `info` in every deployed environment\n- [ ] `local.yaml` keeps `LOG_LEVEL: debug`\n- [ ] `scripts/tests/config.test.mjs` asserts the level per file"},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
// Scope pair, open side: only `ci.yaml` is added. It is neither local nor stated as deployed, and the per-file assertion forces a choice the issue does not make (B3 "which environments?").
{"id":"invalid-scope-environment-open","tags":["invalid","b3","scope-pair"],"input":{"title":"[CHORE] Disable debug logging in deployed environments","body":"`LOG_LEVEL=debug` leaks request bodies. `config/env/` holds `local.yaml`, `ci.yaml`, `preview.yaml`, `staging.yaml`, `production.yaml`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `LOG_LEVEL` is `info` in every deployed environment\n- [ ] `local.yaml` keeps `LOG_LEVEL: debug`\n- [ ] `scripts/tests/config.test.mjs` asserts the level per file"},"expected":{"valid":false,"blockers":["B3"]}}
// B4 pair (1/3), nothing: the service does not exist, no ticket, no contract, no stub (B4 "AND there is no stub, mock, or documented workaround").
{"id":"invalid-b4-pair-none","tags":["invalid","b4","stub"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Show model cost in the PR review comment","body":"Append the review's cost to the comment posted by `scripts/pr_review.mjs`, from the per-model prices of the pricing service. The pricing service is not deployed yet.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The comment ends with `Cost: $<usd>`: input tokens × input price + output tokens × output price (prices per million tokens), rounded to 4 decimals\n- [ ] Prices are fetched once per run\n- [ ] A test in `scripts/tests/pr_review.test.mjs` asserts the line for 1,000 input and 500 output tokens"},"expected":{"valid":false,"blockers":["B4"]}}
