{"id":"invalid-b4-pair-ticket","tags":["invalid","b4","stub"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Show model cost in the PR review comment","body":"Append the review's cost to the comment posted by `scripts/pr_review.mjs`, from the per-model prices of the pricing service. The pricing service is not deployed yet. It is tracked in PLAT-430; its contract is published in `docs/contracts.md#pricing`: `GET /prices/:model` → 200 `{ inputPerMTok, outputPerMTok }`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The comment ends with `Cost: $<usd>`: input tokens × input price + output tokens × output price (prices per million tokens), rounded to 4 decimals\n- [ ] Prices are fetched once per run\n- [ ] A test in `scripts/tests/pr_review.test.mjs` asserts the line for 1,000 input and 500 output tokens"},"expected":{"valid":false,"blockers":["B4"]}}
// B4 pair (3/3), stub, no ticket: B4 NOT BLOCKED "explicitly mocked/stubbed for this implementation". The only valid side of the pair.
{"id":"valid-b4-pair-stub","tags":["valid","b4","stub"],"input":{"title":"[FEATURE] Show model cost in the PR review comment","body":"Append the review's cost to the comment posted by `scripts/pr_review.mjs`, from the per-model prices of the pricing service. The pricing service is not deployed yet. Until it ships, `scripts/lib/pricing_stub.mjs` exports `getPrice(model)` returning `{ inputPerMTok: 0.15, outputPerMTok: 0.6 }`, and `pr_review.mjs` reads prices through it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The comment ends with `Cost: $<usd>`: input tokens × input price + output tokens × output price (prices per million tokens), rounded to 4 decimals\n- [ ] Prices are fetched once per run\n- [ ] A test in `scripts/tests/pr_review.test.mjs` asserts the line for 1,000 input and 500 output tokens"},"expected":{"valid":true,"score_min":70}}
